  "slug": "codes-distance-49c0",
  "summary": "New preprints target circuit distance, leakage, loss and magic-state fault distance directly, rather than nominal code parameters, for practical QEC.",
  "synthesis": "The dominant thread is that fault-tolerance performance is set by how faults propagate through concrete circuits, not by nominal code distance. The singlet-flag scheme restores circuit distance for shuttled qLDPC codes in silicon, lowering logical error rates 2-10x. CP-SAT synthesis of syndrome-extraction circuits for CSS qLDPC codes reduces logical error rates. Block Checks with a Pareto tree search improve depth–operation trade-offs for fault-tolerant state preparation. The cultivation analysis gives an exact theory of harmful faults and shows that S-gate proxies overstate the fault distance of T-gate cultivation. Non-Pauli noise also features prominently: foliated surface codes are shown optimal against space- and time-like skip-gate leakage, and Ellis provides fast exact Pauli-frame simulation under qubit loss. Alongside these, code-construction work covers high-rate small color codes, ancilla-free code quilts for logical Pauli-product measurements, and CSS-T-Product codes for tailored magic-state factories.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-opus-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-25"
}
